<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince Albert, Duke of Teschen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1738">1738</a>–<a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Albert of Saxe-Teschen, Albert Casimir of Saxony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince Albert, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Teschen</a>, was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augustus-iii">Augustus III</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> who married Archduchess Maria Christina, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a>, and received the Duchy of Cieszyn in 1766. He governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and assembled the great collection of drawings and prints now held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-konigsberg">Albertina</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-albert-duke-of-teschen.jpg" alt="Prince Albert, Duke of Teschen" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcello Bacciarelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marcello_Bacciarelli_-_Albert_Kazimierz_Sasko-Cieszy%C5%84ski_1766.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
